{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3905316","formula":"C₁₂H₁₄N₂O","hill":"C12H14N2O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":12.0,"H":14.0,"N":2.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Pinoline"},"descriptions":{"en":"Pinoline, also known as 6-methoxytryptoline or as 6-methoxy-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-β-carboline (6-MeO-THβC), is a β-carboline long-claimed to be produced in the pineal gland during the metabolism of melatonin, however its pineal occurrence remains controversial. Its more common name is a contraction of \"pineal β-carboline\". The biological activity of this molecule is of interest as a potential free radical scavenger, also known as an antioxidant, and as a monoamine oxidase A inhibitor."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":1868,"mass":202.25,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=CC2=C(C=C1)NC3=C2CCNC3","inchikey":"QYMDEOQLJUUNOF-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"6-methoxy-2,3,4,9-tetrahydro-1H-pyrido[3,4-b]indole","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"1868","atoms":29,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.846,"y":0.727,"z":0.021,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.029,"y":-1.796,"z":-0.028,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.946,"y":0.511,"z":0.355,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.128,"y":0.428,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.877,"y":-0.728,"z":-0.011,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.786,"y":1.764,"z":0.033,"el":"C"},{"x":0.242,"y":0.052,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.361,"y":-0.791,"z":-0.034,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.282,"y":1.636,"z":-0.337,"el":"C"},{"x":0.277,"y":-1.348,"z":-0.02,"el":"C"},{"x":1.46,"y":0.76,"z":0.015,"el":"C"},{"x":1.475,"y":-2.07,"z":-0.029,"el":"C"},{"x":2.665,"y":0.048,"z":0.007,"el":"C"},{"x":2.67,"y":-1.345,"z":-0.015,"el":"C"},{"x":3.775,"y":2.151,"z":0.043,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.693,"y":2.18,"z":1.044,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.294,"y":2.454,"z":-0.66,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.701,"y":-1.059,"z":-1.042,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.723,"y":-1.559,"z":0.658,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.793,"